    "title": "Scammers Impersonate Church Leaders in New Digital Fraud Schemes - NewsBreak",
    "text": "5 days ago This article contains content summarized with GPT-4. Learn more.\nChurches across the United States are dealing with new digital scams. Fraudsters are impersonating church leaders to take advantage of congregation members. These scams often involve emails or messages that appear to be from trusted individuals. Scammers may ask for money or sensitive information. Security experts say that awareness and verification are key to preventing these incidents. Churches are encouraged to educate their members and use security measures to reduce the risk of fraud.\nvideo by @PleasantGreen\n5",
